  "preamble": "Fortition of the voiced velar fricative [ɣ] to the stop [ɡ]. The clearest case is Germanic: Proto-Germanic *g was a fricative [ɣ] except after nasals and in geminates, and word-initially it hardened to [ɡ] in Old Norse and, before back vowels and consonants, in Old English (Proto-Germanic *gōdaz /ˈɣɔː.ðɑz/ > Old Norse góðr, Old English gōd).",
